Z||000008||theogre||04-20-2000||08:18 PM||||Those look nice.<P>I'm guessing you're using Testor's model paint. It's been my notice that the metal flake ones, like gold & silver, don't last really well. The solid colors hold up to allot of abuse, but the flakes start looking ratty if they get handled much.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||04-20-2000||11:34 PM||||Ogre, These are Epoxy paints. The silver is actually called Aluminum. They are 2-part paints from "HYSOL" (brand name) They don't chip or fade like model paint. Also I clear coat them with a urethane clear coat to give them an even high gloss shine. <BR>Pegasus, They don't have a burgundy, sorry.<BR>Most colors they have are your basic colors plus aluminum and gold. I could probably mix the black and red or blue and red and see if I can get a burgundy color.||||reg||1
